  "worked_solution": "Let's add $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254493/assets/9a82654748f7c41d814fa06abfc2ac9b552912d25559ba3020559befd31b61d5.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $4$ units **down**.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4.$",
